# Root .gitignore of the repo (allowlist): only our own code (tools, resources and framework).
#
# Allowlist: EVERYTHING is left out except what is named below with "!". This way a new folder (data, dumps,
# diagnostics, sandbox...) never gets in by accident. To version something new, add it here on purpose.
#
# framework\ is a fork of SuperMarioWonderRecomp (MIT) and lives inside this repo; what is already versioned stays tracked.
# Never versioned: data\ (dumps, romfs, exefs, gen\, analysis\, spirv\, fonts, saves), dumps\, keys.

# ---- everything out by default ----
/*

# ---- what does get in ----

# input.ini.example (FSN-style example): only this file inside framework\
!/framework/
/framework/*
!/framework/games/
/framework/games/*
!/framework/games/tsukihime_common/
/framework/games/tsukihime_common/*
!/framework/games/tsukihime_common/input.ini.example

!/.gitignore
!/.gitattributes
!/LICENSE
!/NOTICE.md
!/README.md

# tools\: only scripts and patches (not nstool.exe or Python cache)
!/tools/
/tools/*
!/tools/*.ps1
!/tools/*.py
# subfolders by purpose: internal (called by recomp), patches (apply_*.py, already applied in
# framework\), dev (analysis), tests
!/tools/internal/
!/tools/patches/
!/tools/dev/
!/tools/tests/
# nsextract (C#, LibHac): only the sources are tracked (not bin\ or obj\)
!/tools/nsextract/
/tools/nsextract/*
!/tools/nsextract/nsextract.csproj
!/tools/nsextract/Program.cs
# tools\linux\: building from Linux (.sh wrappers, CMake toolchain)
!/tools/linux/
/tools/linux/*
!/tools/linux/*.sh
!/tools/linux/*.cmake
!/tools/linux/*.ps1
!/tools/linux/*.py
# personal (paths of one PC): never in the repo
/tools/dev.local.ps1

# ---- HUD button icons by device (AP_HUD_GLYPHS) ----
# tools\hud: the scripts recomp_tsukihime.ps1 runs (build_hud_assets.py and what it imports; slice_sheet.py, which
# made utils\hud_sliced from the Figma sheets, stays local). utils\: only the icons those scripts read (credits in
# resources\HUD-LICENSES.md): the Xbox and PlayStation slices the atlases and the controls table use, and the filled
# keyboard keys input.ini can name. Everything else there (source sheets, mouse icons, previews, outputs) stays local.
!/tools/hud/
/tools/hud/*
!/tools/hud/*.py
/tools/hud/slice_sheet.py
!/framework/games/tsukihime_common/hud_glyphs.cpp
!/framework/games/tsukihime_common/hud_glyphs.h
!/utils/
/utils/*
!/utils/hud_sliced/
/utils/hud_sliced/*
!/utils/hud_sliced/xbox/
/utils/hud_sliced/xbox/*
!/utils/hud_sliced/xbox/xbox_r00_c04.png
